### Step 3: JavaScript to Detect Viewport Entry

Use the `Intersection Observer` API to detect when the element enters the viewport.

```javascript
// Get all elements you want to observe
const elements = document.querySelectorAll('.animatable');

// Define the observer configuration
const config = {
    root: null, // Default root (the viewport)
    threshold: [0] // Trigger when any part of the element is visible
};

// Create an IntersectionObserver instance
const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(entry => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
            // Apply the animation when the element is in view
            entry.target.classList.add('is-visible');
            // Stop observing once the animation is applied
            observer.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
    });
}, config);

// Start observing each element
elements.forEach(element => {
    observer.observe(element);
});
```

### Step 4: CSS for Animation

Finally, define the CSS for the animated state.

```css
